  "hints": [
    "a palindrome is symmetric around some center - what if instead of checking every substring, you tried every possible center and grew outward as long as both sides matched?",
    "there are 2n-1 possible centers: n single-character centers (odd-length palindromes) and n-1 between-character centers (even-length palindromes)",
    "for each center, expand left and right pointers outward one step at a time while s[left] == s[right], stopping as soon as they mismatch or go out of bounds",
    "track the best (longest) palindrome found so far, and only replace it when a strictly longer one is found, which naturally preserves the earliest-starting tie-break"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "forgetting to check even-length palindromes (centers between two characters), only checking odd-length ones",
    "replacing the best answer on a tie (equal length) instead of only on strictly longer, which breaks the leftmost tie-break rule",
    "off-by-one errors when converting the expand-around-center left/right pointers back into a substring"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a string `s`.\n\n**Find the longest contiguous substring of `s` that reads the same\nforwards and backwards.**\n\nIf more than one substring achieves the maximum length, return the one\nthat starts at the smallest index, so the result is always uniquely\ndetermined.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= s.length <= 1000",
      "s consists of digits and English letters only",
      "if multiple longest palindromic substrings exist, return the one starting at the smallest index"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "the entire string itself is a palindrome",
      "no palindrome longer than a single character exists",
      "an even-length palindrome (center falls between two characters) versus an odd-length one (center on a single character)"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s = \"babad\"",
        "output": "\"bab\"",
        "expectedOutput": "\"bab\"",
        "explanation": "\"aba\" is also a valid palindrome of length 3, but \"bab\" starts earlier (index 0 vs index 1), so it is returned"
      },
      {
